    <string name="help_idea_t">The idea</string>
    <string name="help_idea">A single-table no-limit Texas hold\'em tournament for 2 to 9 friends. Everyone starts with 5,000 chips; blinds rise every 10 minutes; the last player with chips wins.</string>
    <string name="help_join_t">Rooms</string>
    <string name="help_join">Pick the Casino or the Home room. Anyone at a room can add computer players and start. Whoever starts is the host for the whole game. Join a running game to watch.</string>
    <string name="help_play_t">Playing a hand</string>
    <string name="help_play">You have 30 seconds for each decision. Tap Fold, Check or Call, or drag the slider to bet or raise. If time runs out you check when that is free, otherwise you fold.</string>
    <string name="help_rebuy_t">One rebuy</string>
    <string name="help_rebuy">Lose all your chips in a hand dealt at level 1, 2 or 3 and you are offered one rebuy of 5,000 within 30 seconds. After that, or if you decline, you are out.</string>
    <string name="help_pause_t">Pauses and leaving</string>
    <string name="help_pause">If the host leaves or loses connection the game pauses for everyone until they are back. Anyone else leaving keeps their seat and chips and can come back. The host can pause between hands. Any player still in can end the game for everyone; then nobody wins.</string>
    <string name="help_video_t">Video</string>
    <string name="help_video">Camera and microphone connect when you sit down. Tap the toggles to switch them off. Computer-only games keep them off.</string>
    <string name="help_footer">Standard tournament rules: dead button, minimum raise equals the last full raise, odd chips go clockwise from the button.</string>
