    <string name="tut_home_t">Welcome to OurPoker</string>
    <string name="tut_home_rooms">Each room is a poker table: Casino and Home. Up to nine players sit at one, friends and computer players.</string>
    <string name="tut_home_preview">Tap a room to select it and see what it looks like.</string>
    <string name="tut_home_enter">Tap the arrow to sit down in the selected room. If a game is already on there, you watch it.</string>
    <string name="tut_home_name">Tap the pencil to change the name the others see.</string>
    <string name="tut_lobby_t">The waiting room</string>
    <string name="tut_lobby_room">Everyone listed here plays the next game together.</string>
    <string name="tut_lobby_bots">Add a computer player with the robot button.</string>
    <string name="tut_lobby_start">Anyone can press play to start the game once two players are here.</string>
    <string name="tut_lobby_exit">The arrow on the left takes you out. When the last person leaves, the room is cleared, computer players too.</string>
    <string name="tut_bots_t">Computer players</string>
    <string name="tut_bots_mark">A robot marks a computer player.</string>
    <string name="tut_bots_remove">Tap the minus beside one to remove it.</string>
    <string name="tut_table_t">The table</string>
    <string name="tut_table_board">The middle row holds the community cards, shared by everyone. Each place is underlined gold.</string>
    <string name="tut_table_pot">The pot ring collects the chips bet in each round. The winner of the hand takes it all.</string>
    <string name="tut_table_level">Above the prompt: the level, the blinds and the time until they rise.</string>
    <string name="tut_cards_t">Your cards and chips</string>
    <string name="tut_cards_hand">Your two cards are underlined green. When it is your turn they glow: double tap them to check, flick them up to fold.</string>
    <string name="tut_cards_stack">Tap your chips to bet or raise; tap Call to match the bet.</string>
    <string name="tut_cards_zoom">Tap any cards to see them large; tap again to put them away.</string>
    <string name="tut_odds_list">Under the table: the hands your cards can still make, most likely first, with the chance of each.</string>
    <string name="tut_odds_box">The cards that make a hand sit in a dotted box; the cards after it only settle ties.</string>
    <string name="tut_odds_colours">Underlines show where each card comes from: green your hand, gold the community cards, red still to come.</string>
    <string name="tut_odds_rank">#1 is the best hand there is, a royal flush; every hand beats all the hands ranked below it.</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_blinds_t">The blinds</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_blinds">Every hand starts with two forced bets: the small blind and the big blind, twice as much. They move one seat round the table each hand and rise with each level.</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_call_t">Calling</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_call">To call is to put in as much as the highest bet so far, to stay in the hand.</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_bet_t">Betting and raising</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_bet">A bet puts in chips that everyone else must match to stay in; a raise makes the bet bigger.</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_pot_t">The pot</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_pot">When a round of betting ends, the bets go into the pot. The best hand at the end, or the last player left, takes it.</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_flop_t">The flop</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_flop">Three community cards are turned up together: the flop. Another round of betting follows.</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_turn_t">The turn</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_turn">A fourth community card: the turn. Then another round of betting.</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_river_t">The river</string>
    <string name="tut_ev_river">The fifth and last community card: the river. After the last round of betting, the hands are shown.</string>
